{"name":"Van Cleef","hex":"#523936","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Van Cleef","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Dutch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Van_Cleef"}],"entries":[{"title":"Van Cleef","blocks":[{"text":"Van Cleef is a Dutch surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["Jan Van Cleef (1646–1716), Flemish painter","Joos van Cleve (1485–1540), painter from Cleves","Cornelius van Cleve (1520–1567), painter and son of Joos","Lee Van Cleef (1925–1989), American film actor who primarily starred in westerns","June Van Cleef, American photographer","Nathan van Cleef, one of the villains of Shanghai Noon"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Cleef"},{"title":"Van","blocks":[{"text":"A van is a type of road vehicle used for transporting goods or people. There is some variation in the scope of the word across the different English-speaking countries. The smallest vans, microvans, are used for transporting either goods or people in tiny quantities. Mini MPVs, compact MPVs, and MPVs are all small vans usually used for transporting people in small quantities. Larger vans with passenger seats are used for institutional purposes, such as transporting students. Larger vans with only front seats are often used for business purposes, to carry goods and equipment. Specially equipped vans are used by television stations as mobile studios. Postal services and courier companies use large step vans to deliver packages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2018_Ford_Transit_Custom_300_Base_2.0_facelift.jpg/330px-2018_Ford_Transit_Custom_300_Base_2.0_facelift.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg/500px-Roger_Fenton%27s_waggon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa